# Docker build context = repo root for BOTH backend and frontend images (see
# docker-compose.yml, todos los servicios usan `context: .`) — pnpm/turbo
# necesitan ver el workspace completo (apps/backend + apps/frontend +
# packages) para resolver dependencias compartidas (@repo/ui,
# @repo/backend-commons) sin importar qué Dockerfile se esté corriendo. Keep
# this list conservative: excluding something the pnpm install / prisma
# generate / turbo build steps need will fail the build, so when in doubt,
# don't exclude it.

.git

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/coverage

# Stale TypeScript incremental-build caches must never ride along into a
# Docker build: if present without a matching dist/, tsc treats the project
# as already up to date and silently emits nothing (0 files, exit 0). This
# has actually happened in this repo (auth-service/core-service committed
# tsconfig.build.tsbuildinfo files) — always force a full compile in images.
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Misc repo housekeeping not needed to build/run any service.
docs
.planning
.claude
.github
infra
*.md
.env
.env.*

# Llaves RSA (RS256/JWKS): nunca deben quedar horneadas en una capa de imagen.
# auth-service las recibe por volumen en runtime (docker-compose.yml), no por COPY.
keys
*.pem
